{
  "dom_id": "step-q183282",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\,$ **If** you are not sick, **then** you don't go to the hospital.",
  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ You are not sick.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You don't go to the hospital.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\n¬A⇒¬B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B:$\n\n- $¬A:$ You are sick.\n\n- $¬B:$ You go to the hospital.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you are sick, then you go to the hospital.",
